# Telemetry → canvas update

Playbook or startup telemetry work is **not done** until the appropriate canvas reflects the new runs — not when traces exist only on disk.

## Pick the canvas

| Work | Canvas (Cursor managed path) |
|------|------------------------------|
| **S1–S7, F1–F10** playbook baselines | `C:\Users\tilou\.cursor\projects\c-Coding-projects-Obsidian-Seek\canvases\sandbox-run-history.canvas.tsx` |
| Startup track probes (T0–T6, worktrees) | `…/canvases/startup-tracks.canvas.tsx` or `startup-report.canvas.tsx` |
| Architecture / design only | `docs/seek-architecture.canvas.tsx` — **do not** append RUNS here |

When unsure, default to **sandbox-run-history** for anything dispatched via `run-scenario.ps1` or `run-all-scenarios.ps1`.

## Before editing

1. Read the canvas skill: `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/canvas/SKILL.md`.
2. Read the target `.canvas.tsx` — match existing `SandboxRun` / `RUNS[]` shape and any embedded distribution constants (e.g. `F3_RUN_LATENCIES_MS`).
3. Pull metrics from authoritative artifacts:
   - `.cursor/functional-traces/<Id>/`
   - `.cursor/gate-trace.jsonl`
   - `.cursor/scorecards/` (when present)
   - Driver stdout / `.cursor/playbook-run-failures.md`

## What to update

- **`RUNS[]`** — append or replace bad runs after discard; one entry per sample with `scenarioId`, `outcome`, `metrics`, `gitSha`, `artifacts`, `protocolSteps`.
- **Deviation charts** — when multiple runs exist for a scenario, refresh violin/KDE inputs (per-run latency arrays, S6 `namePartialMs`, F2 `T_first_good_ms`, etc.). Do not leave stale distributions after a new batch.
- **Overview stats** — derive from `RUNS`; do not hand-maintain counts that contradict traces.
- **Stub scenarios** — leave pending; do not fabricate RUNS for `status: stub` drivers.

Use `Emit-CanvasRunJson.ps1` field names as the schema reference. Prefer editing the canvas file directly over telling the user to paste JSON.

## Do not

- Commit canvas files (outside git repo).
- Render empty chart sections — omit or hide when `n = 0`.
- Use hardcoded hex colors — `useHostTheme()` / `theme.category` only.
- Skip canvas update because `playbook-run-failures.md` was written — the markdown log and canvas serve different purposes.

## Finish check

- Canvas TypeScript check reports no errors.
- User can open the canvas beside chat and see the new run(s) and deviation plots for scenarios with `n ≥ 2` samples.
- After `run-all-scenarios.ps1`, run `export-canvas-baseline.ps1` then splice `gen-canvas-ts-block.py` output into `sandbox-run-history.canvas.tsx` (or hand-update `RUNS` + `SCENARIO_VIOLIN`).
- **3-sample baselines:** full drivers should show `n=3` in overview table and one **error-bar chart** per test id with y-axis range local to that scenario only (do not pool S6/F3/S1/F2 on one axis).
